  "stem": "The expression \\((x^{2} + 3x - 2)(x - 4)\\) is equivalent to \\(x^{3} + ax^{2} + bx + 8\\), where \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) are constants. What is the value of \\(b\\)?",
  "figure": null,
  "answer_type": "spr",
  "choices": null,
  "answer": null,
  "spr_answers": [
    "-14"
  ],
  "solution": [
    "The \\(x\\)-terms come from \\(3x \\cdot (-4)\\) and \\(-2 \\cdot x\\).",
    "\\(-12x - 2x = -14x\\), so \\(b = -14\\).",
    "(The full product is \\(x^{3} - x^{2} - 14x + 8\\).)"
  ],
  "explanation": null,
  "traps": null,
  "verify": "x = symbols('x')\np = Poly(expand((x**2 + 3*x - 2)*(x - 4)), x)\nassert p.coeff_monomial(1) == 8 and p.coeff_monomial(x**3) == 1\nassert p.coeff_monomial(x) == -14\nassert [Rational(v) for v in spr_answers] == [-14]",
